WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.469
Who doesn’t love a party, right?

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:06.800
A lot of us jump at the chance to leave all
our troubles behind and get together with

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.780
friends and family for a good time, celebrating
a special occasion while unencumbered by the

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.950
weighty responsibilities of everyday life.

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:21.460
Parties give us an excuse to kick back, to
meet new people as well as catch up with old

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:27.170
acquaintances, and mark a holiday or someone’s
birthday in the most memorable way possible.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:32.450
Or at least, they can be when you’re one
of the guests invited to a party.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:37.600
But when you happen to be one of the poor
souls tasked with organizing one, they can

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:43.120
change from an exciting and much-anticipated
social gathering to a dreaded time-sink of

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.320
organizational and logistical chaos.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.570
Can you tell I needed to organize O5-1’s
141st birthday party recently?

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.851
I’m still recovering from the stress…

00:00:53.851 --> 00:00:57.800
But I’m not the only one suffering from
this particular kind of anxiety.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:03.769
For a young man named Alex, planning an upcoming
shindig was turning out to be that particular

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:09.299
kind of absolute nightmare that anyone who
has ever tried to organize a party will be

00:01:09.299 --> 00:01:11.320
all too familiar with.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:16.320
It had seemed like such a long time away when
Alex had first drawn that short and oh-so

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:17.799
unlucky straw.

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:22.759
Two months, on paper it sounds like forever,
plenty of time to get everything ready.

00:01:22.759 --> 00:01:27.720
But the list of jobs that needed doing before
the dreaded party date only seemed to get

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.140
longer and more complicated with each day
that passed.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:36.360
You see, normally Alex thrived at keeping
himself organized, every part of his life

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.250
usually running like clockwork.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:43.030
The trick, as he’d found, was to pay attention
to what he could control.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:47.049
Naturally, in life, the unexpected usually
tends to happen.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:52.790
But Alex had learned that by regimenting his
daily routine, having specific times for certain

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.770
tasks, and scheduling the week’s events
on his calendar, he could keep himself pretty

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.439
on top of everything.

00:01:59.439 --> 00:02:04.119
It was that organizational mindset that meant
that Alex’s friends decided to nominate

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:09.140
him as the sole planner for an upcoming surprise
birthday party.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.281
Of course, being organized and in control
of one’s own life goes completely out of

00:02:13.281 --> 00:02:18.280
the window when trying to coordinate all the
various moving parts needed for a party.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:23.000
It had been left up to Alex to sort out where
this celebration was going to be held along

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.890
with who would be attending, the entertainment,
food and drink, setting up group chats to

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:34.230
update everyone, along with a whole cavalcade
of other important party factors, each one

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:36.950
fraught with its own potential problems.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.240
From the beginning, it was an uphill battle.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.590
The first venue Alex had booked had to cancel;
the whole building needed to be fumigated

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.760
because of a rat problem.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.670
Guests were RSVPing at a sporadic rate, some
would confirm their attendance, only to back

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:51.770
out days later.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:56.540
With the party date drawing closer and closer,
the planning had become a perfect storm of

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.750
problems that were all out of Alex’s hands.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:05.340
In an effort to regain some control, he raced
out only a week before the party, stocking

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:09.400
up on finger foods and beverages that were
all extremely overpriced.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:15.690
But by now, the party was only a few days
away and Alex was acting in a blind panic.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:21.090
You see, it was in that panic that he reached
for something, throwing it into his shopping

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.340
cart without fully thinking about it.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.510
It was a piñata, a hollow, paper mâché
animal designed to be filled with candy and

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.830
hit with sticks until the contents burst out.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:37.220
Sure, it was a childish party game, and in
the back of his mind, Alex wasn’t sure why

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.760
he’d picked it up.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:44.430
Maybe part of him thought everyone would find
it amusing, a bit of quaint, nostalgic entertainment.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.910
He barely noticed how it didn’t even seem
to resemble any known animal and was instead

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:52.850
shaped like a strange cross between a unicorn
and a llama.

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:58.000
Alex was too lost in everything else he still
had to do to think about the piñata for too

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.000
long.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.070
His biggest mistake was deciding not to put
it back in the corner of the party store where

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:04.210
he’d found it.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:08.790
Arranging for the surprise to take place at
one of his friend’s houses, Alex’s party

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.070
seemed to be coming together at long last.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:16.100
But still, he was in a state of panic, with
only a rough estimate of how many people were

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:20.110
going to be there and no clue who might show
up or not.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:25.160
Gradually, the guests filled in, and the more
of them that did arrive only caused Alex further

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.340
worry that he hadn’t bought enough food
and drink.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:34.470
Much to his frustration, a few who had canceled
managed to change their other plans last-minute,

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:38.000
and made it despite saying they wouldn’t
be able to.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:43.290
Despite everything coming together, the whole
event still felt like an unmitigated disaster.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:47.411
Even after the guest of honor arrived, the
surprise was sprung and the evening was in

00:04:47.411 --> 00:04:51.040
full swing, Alex’s brain was still in organization
mode.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:55.820
If a drink got spilled, he dashed in and mopped
it up to avoid any lasting mess.

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:59.740
The same happened if food was dropped or chairs
were knocked over.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:04.050
Truth be told, it was actually stopping Alex
from being able to enjoy the party he'd spent

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.730
so much effort organizing.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.150
“That’s your problem, man!”

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:09.900
Milo, one of his friends, told him.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:15.950
“This is a party, stop trying to control
everything, stop worrying and you never know,

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.970
you might just have some fun tonight!”

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:21.530
“I suppose you’re right,” Alex sighed
a reply.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:24.500
“No way, you got a piñata?”

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:28.570
Milo had spotted the brightly-colored animal
covered in what looked like tissue paper.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:32.900
Instantly, Alex felt embarrassed that he’d
picked it up, fully expecting to be a laughing

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.150
stock for bringing it to the party.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.330
Surely everyone here had outgrown a party
game like that?

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:43.700
And yet, to Alex’s complete surprise, minutes
later his friends were taking turns being

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:48.840
blindfolded and swiping at the piñata with
a bat, trying to break it open so its candy

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:51.370
contents would come spilling out.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:56.091
As he watched Milo take a huge swing and miss
the piñata by a mile, Alex couldn’t help

00:05:56.091 --> 00:06:01.380
but laugh, not even noticing himself relaxing
and enjoying the night’s celebrations.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.920
Soon enough, it was Alex’s turn to be blindfolded.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:10.000
Eyes covered, spun around, unable to see anything
but total darkness, he took a wide swing at

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.100
the piñata.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.100
Miss.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:16.480
Pulling back the bat, spurred on by the chorus
of his friends laughing around him, he gave

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:17.800
it another go.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:23.270
This time he felt it hit, the vibrations traveling
down the bat and into his hands told him it

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.270
had connected.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:29.600
Aiming blindly for the same spot, Alex gave
another swing, this time with much more power

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:34.030
behind it, certain he’d break open the candy-filled
cardboard creature.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:38.670
The bat connected again, hard enough to knock
the piñata off the string keeping it in the

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:39.670
air.

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:43.440
Hearing his friends cheer and whoop, Alex
lifted the blindfold to see the piñata lying

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.860
on the ground a few meters away, then turned
to the group around him.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.990
“One more to break it open?” he asked,
met with laughs and nods of approval.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:56.810
Lifting the bat again, Alex brought it swiping
down towards the piñata with, he was sure,

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.620
enough force to break it open.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.540
But as he struck it, something strange happened.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.860
Or rather, what was strange was that nothing
happened.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.800
The piñata still didn’t break.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.240
It shouldn’t have been possible - after
all, Alex was sure it had only been made of

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:14.020
flimsy cardboard and paper mâché.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:15.950
The whole thing should have come apart by
now.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:21.090
And yet, the bat had lazily glanced off the
piñata, the inanimate animal seemed to resist

00:07:21.090 --> 00:07:23.770
the oncoming bat as if it was nothing.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:27.860
By now, the other guests at the party were
looking somewhat bemused at Alex.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.950
They too had been expecting the piñata to
break, and a shower of the candy within to

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:33.120
come spilling out.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.490
Not wanting to lose face, Alex made the instinctive
decision to take one final swing at it…

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:40.450
only to find he couldn’t.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:45.240
His arm wasn’t moving; it had, less than
thirty seconds ago, he’d been able to lift

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:49.000
his arm but now it was rigid, locked in place.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:54.460
Alex’s lower body was in much the same state,
unable to move as if his feet had been stuck

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:58.139
to the ground, legs too stiff to take a step.

00:07:58.139 --> 00:08:02.660
The only part of his body Alex could still
move were his eyes, which now darted franticly

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.190
over the faces of the party guests.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:09.419
Their looks of bemusement or excited smiles
were all rapidly washing away into stares

00:08:09.419 --> 00:08:11.680
of confusion and concern.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.340
Some of his friends started asking what was
wrong, but he couldn’t reply.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:20.881
When Alex tried to speak, his jaw stayed clenched
shut, teeth pushed together so hard that they

00:08:20.881 --> 00:08:24.699
might shatter, tongue and tonsils frozen still.

00:08:24.699 --> 00:08:28.960
Some of the guests drew closer, waving hands
and clicking fingers in front of Alex’s

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:32.070
face, trying to elicit some kind of movement
from him.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:36.110
A few thought it was a joke, waiting for him
to suddenly move and shout and frighten them

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.539
for a cheap laugh.

00:08:37.539 --> 00:08:42.430
All the while, Alex was trapped in his own
skin, locked in a body that had somehow become

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:45.330
a prison the moment he’d stepped closer
to the piñata.

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:50.380
His eyes caught sight of Milo, dashing into
another room and returning with a phone in

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.380
hand.

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:55.710
He punched in three numbers to call the emergency
services, although it did little to calm the

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:58.160
rampant internal panic Alex was feeling.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.480
The paramedics arrived at a record speed.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.390
By the time the ambulance pulled up at the
house, most of the other party guests had

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:09.089
either stepped way back from Alex – still
standing frozen in place – or had left the

00:09:09.089 --> 00:09:10.440
party altogether.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:15.640
As the EMT’s rushed in and started asking
if he could hear them or say anything, Alex

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:18.890
tried with every ounce of strength to get
his mouth to move.

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:23.850
“Yes,” he wanted to say, to scream, just
to let all the mounting panic out.

00:09:23.850 --> 00:09:25.620
“I can hear you!

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.840
I’m awake, I’m in here!

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.620
I just can’t move.”

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:34.210
Despite their best efforts, the paramedics
couldn’t get Alex to move, instead trying

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:37.350
to lay his rigid body down to begin CPR.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:41.600
One of them gripped his hands together, about
to start chest compressions while everyone

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.920
still at the party watched in silence.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:49.210
The paramedic gently pushed down on Alex’s
chest when, just like a piñata, it burst

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:50.210
open.

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:55.050
For a microsecond, Alex’s eyes widened in
pain and shock, before rolling back.

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:59.940
His chest split, as if it was made of paper
mâché instead of skin and bone.

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:04.130
Inside, where his lungs should have been,
was a pile of candy.

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:08.760
The party didn’t end with a bang that night,
but with a horrified scream.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:13.190
Later that night, after the rest of the party’s
guests either fled home or were urged to leave

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:17.850
by the confused paramedics, the police were
called to the scene, roping off the room where

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.420
the apparent ‘accident’ had happened.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:24.670
Although curiously, it seemed that the piñata
had somehow vanished.

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:29.270
Maybe someone removed it, after all, it’s
not like it just got up and walked away, right?

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:33.480
Meanwhile, Alex’s remains were taken to
the local mortuary and handed over to the

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.570
pathologists for an autopsy.

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:41.050
They noticed, despite only having died recently,
the body seemed to be severely dehydrated,

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:45.880
to the point where the limbs, the outer skin,
and various internal organs were brittle;

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:50.399
The pathologists that examined the body made
another startling and confusing discovery

00:10:50.399 --> 00:10:52.960
when they opened up what was left of Alex.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:58.089
More candy was growing out of his organs;
there were over a thousand sugary pieces,

00:10:58.089 --> 00:11:03.290
each one individually wrapped in unmarked
foil, without any logos or branding.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:08.040
Needless to say, the pathologists examining
Alex’s corpse were understandably left baffled;

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:12.880
they had never seen anything like this in
any cadaver, barely able to come up with a

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:13.900
cause of death.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:17.860
How had his body gone rigid and left him completely
unable to move?

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:21.940
How had candy been able to start growing from
his internal organs?

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:27.260
And, most importantly, who or what had done
this to Alex?

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.720
Well, here’s what happened.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:33.830
Something that Alex had presumed to be nothing
more than a harmless party favor filled with

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:37.930
delicious treats was far from just an ordinary
piñata.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.850
You see, it was actually an instance of SCP-956.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:46.220
Although, we can hardly hold Alex entirely
at fault for assuming there was nothing different

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.500
about this particular piñata.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:54.410
On the outside, SCP-956 does appear to be
an unassuming cardboard creature made of paper

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:58.310
mâché, or at least that’s what it feels
like it’s made of.

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:06.330
But the surface of SCP-956 is actually constructed
of unidentifiable fur, glue, sugar, and – most

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:09.209
unnervingly – human tissue.

00:12:09.209 --> 00:12:15.040
SCP-956 is an entity that normally remains
in an inactive and docile state, displaying

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:20.520
no intelligence or active hostility.

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:24.670
Unlike any ordinary piñata you might buy
from a local party store – which are designed

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:30.730
to break upon impact – SCP-956 manages to
maintain its structural integrity against

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:33.020
most forms of external damage.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:38.270
Whether bludgeoning it with a bat or applying
crushing force with fists or kicks, the piñata

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:41.080
will show virtually no change in its state.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:45.970
The only effective way to leave any lasting
damage is through the use of flames or gunfire,

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:50.260
and you might have a hard time finding any
of those at your average piñata party.

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:56.330
However, when an unwitting human victim comes
within a five-meter range of SCP-956, and

00:12:56.330 --> 00:13:01.399
for a long enough time, the entity’s further
anomalous qualities will activate.

00:13:01.399 --> 00:13:05.620
The piñata will render its victim totally
paralyzed from head to toe, diminishing their

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:10.850
motor functions and leaving them unable to
move any part of their body, save for their

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:11.850
eyes.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.930
This doesn’t kill the victim, however, just
immobilizes them.

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:19.990
They retain full awareness – just like Alex
did – but can only helplessly look around

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:21.440
while being unable to flee.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.640
And why would they need to flee?

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:30.190
Well, because once it has frozen a victim,
that’s when SCP-956 begins its approach.

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:34.740
The piñata will switch from being an inanimate
object to a creature capable of movement,

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:38.930
and proceeds to physically attack its immobile,
vulnerable human target.

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:44.070
It doesn’t stop, continuously bludgeoning
at the victim until, eventually, their chest

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:48.320
ruptures and a pile of candy comes tumbling
out like an avalanche.

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:53.920
As for why SCP-956 didn’t try to attack
Alex this way, maybe someone else at the party

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:58.640
knocked it aside without noticing, or perhaps
the paramedics managed to make it to the scene

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:01.280
before the piñata had its chance.

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:06.620
Whatever the case, the candy produced by a
victim of SCP-956 seems to be formed using

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:09.400
their internal organs and bodily tissues.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:14.790
It is unclear how quickly this candy begins
growing after a person is exposed to the piñata,

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:18.850
however, it appears that the amount of candy
produced is dependent on how much time the

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:24.980
victim spends in close proximity to SCP-956;
the longer they’re close to it, the more

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:28.430
pieces of candy come spilling out when they’re
opened up.

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:34.130
As for the candy itself – commonly referred
to as SCP-956-1 – as you might expect, it’s

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:37.610
far from anything you’d buy in an ordinary
store.

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:41.519
And its negative effects aren’t just limited
to toothache or sugar rush.

00:14:41.519 --> 00:14:46.130
The pathologists that performed Alex’s post-mortem
were lucky none of them made the grave mistake

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:49.330
of actually eating any of this cursed candy.

00:14:49.330 --> 00:14:55.089
If they had, they could have experienced violent
seizures upon consuming the sugary confectionary.

00:14:55.089 --> 00:14:59.400
Within three minutes, the candy that had come
bursting out of Alex’s insides would have

00:14:59.400 --> 00:15:04.290
made a person drop to the ground unstoppably
convulsing, with a chance that they would

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:08.269
also experience a potentially fatal cardiac
arrest.

00:15:08.269 --> 00:15:14.500
Animals will usually also suffer these effects
upon eating instances of SCP-956-1.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:19.950
In humans, however, the effects of the SCP-956-1
candy seem to vary.

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:25.220
In most cases, those who consume it will experience
the aforementioned seizures with an additional

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:27.580
five percent risk of heart attacks.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:32.120
But other instances have shown an entirely
different side effect that somehow manages

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:34.440
to sound even less appealing.

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:39.080
The second of the candy’s side effects begins
with a process very similar to the immobilization

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:42.420
caused by exposure to SCP-956.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:46.860
A person, after having consumed the candy,
will lose control of their body’s motor

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:49.580
functions, becoming unable to move.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:54.300
However, the first key difference is if they
remain in a standing position, with their

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.480
arms resting in front of their body.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:00.690
The next is the rapid and grotesque sequence
of bodily changes that follow.

00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:05.220
Firstly, their hair rapidly begins to fall
out, shedding in clumps until it is replaced

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:08.680
with paper mâché, that grows over every
inch of skin.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:14.370
Next, their bones and muscles are forcibly
rearranged, crunching and contorting unnaturally

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:18.250
until the affected person can no longer stand
the same way they used to.

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:23.190
In fact, by that point, they aren’t a person
anymore; within nine minutes of eating the

00:16:23.190 --> 00:16:30.360
SCP-956-1 candy, they will have been transformed
from a human being into a piñata.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:35.750
From that moment onwards, they are another
instance of SCP-956.

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:40.339
As you may have already guessed, the Foundation
has done us all a service by rounding up existing

00:16:40.339 --> 00:16:45.670
instances of SCP-956 and all the candy produced
by the pernicious piñata.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:51.180
And that’s a lucky thing too for any of
you would-be party planners out there.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:56.980
After all, nothing is harsher to the celebratory
atmosphere than a piñata that fills people

00:16:56.980 --> 00:17:00.500
with human candy that comes bursting out of
them.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:03.010
Just ask everyone at Alex’s party.

00:17:03.010 --> 00:17:07.839
Although, maybe it’d be a good idea to avoid
buying a piñata for your next get-together,

00:17:07.839 --> 00:17:09.759
just to be on the safe side.

00:17:09.759 --> 00:17:17.029
Now go and check out “SCP-2003 PREFERRED
OPTION” and “SCP-3790 DEPARTMENT OF ABNORMALITIES”

00:17:17.029 --> 00:17:19.589
for more stories to frighten the life out
of your party guests.

